  "title": "Mikhail Gorbachev",
  "summary": "Mikhail Gorbachev (1931-2022), born in Privolnoye in southern Russia, was elected general secretary of the Soviet Communist Party in 1985. At home his glasnost (openness) widened freedom of speech and the press, while perestroika (restructuring) tried to decentralise the economy. Abroad he held summits with Ronald Reagan to limit nuclear arms and end the Cold War, and the Cold War ended peacefully as the Berlin Wall fell in 1989. He won the 1990 Nobel Peace Prize and was the last Soviet leader when the union dissolved in 1991.",
